es are endless, so that would put us on quite the healing treadmill if we have to deal with all the past life trauma now. On the other hand, it could be an excellent therapeutic proxy, perhaps, if it feels too difficult to access the trauma in this life.", null]], "id": "N001"}, {"p": [["Ancestral trauma is another thing a lot of people are now talking about healing. That part is a bit harder to understand because it could mean the trauma that is passed down from generations, which is what everyone is healing essentially even if it's not named that way, or it might mean they are actually trying to heal their ancestors' trauma for their ancestors. If that's the case then I'd say the main validity there is as a loving-kindness practice and another therapeutic proxy technique.", null]], "id": "N001"}, {"p": [["One doorway into either of these would be to do an age regression hypnosis, and just keep going back farther and farther until before you were in your mother's belly.", null]], "id": "N001"}, {"p": [["And you don't necessarily need to have a professional do this either. While age regression to childhood traumas can sometimes be too scary without a professional therapist there to help you, it's often easier to face things from past lives or ancestral stuff, because that's not \"you\" from this life. A professional hypnotist who focuses on past life regressions doesn't have some kind of magic that you lack. In fact, they might be more confused than you, or confuse you, and they usually aren't trauma-informed the way I'd expect someone to be who focuses on childhood trauma. I have one friend, T., who went to a hypnotist to get a past-life regression. He was secretly recording the session so I heard all of it. He was trying to make it work and he felt like he was maybe really remembering his past life as a pirate.", null]], "id": "N001"}, {"p": [["The hypnotist was very much convinced it was real. But afterwards, T. told me he thinks he was just making it all up. My guess is most people tend to err the other way, thinking they weren't making it up. Personally, I don't think it matters if it was a real past life or not unless you're trying to prove it for some other reason, like academic research into past lives. I have ", null], ["more info about rebirth in my nibbana guide", "https://ibogaqueen.substack.com/i/209400477/who-gets-reborn"], [".", null]], "id": "N001"}, {"i": 646}, {"i": 647}, {"i": 648}, {"i": 649}, {"i": 650}, {"i": 651}, {"i": 652}, {"i": 653}, {"i": 654}, {"i": 655}, {"i": 656}, {"i": 657}, {"i": 658}, {"i": 659}, {"i": 660}, {"i": 661}, {"i": 662}, {"i": 663}, {"i": 664}, {"i": 665}, {"i": 666}, {"i": 667}, {"i": 668}, {"i": 669}, {"i": 670}, {"i": 671}, {"i": 672}, {"i": 673}, {"i": 674}, {"i": 675}, {"i": 676}, {"i": 677}, {"i": 678}, {"i": 679}, {"i": 680}, {"i": 681}, {"i": 682}, {"i": 683}, {"i": 684}, {"i": 685}, {"i": 686}, {"i": 687}, {"i": 688}, {"i": 689}, {"i": 690}, {"i": 691}, {"i": 692}, {"i": 693}, {"i": 694}, {"i": 695}, {"i": 696}, {"i": 697}, {"i": 698}, {"i": 699}, {"i": 700}, {"i": 701}, {"i": 702}, {"i": 703}, {"i": 704}, {"i": 705}, {"i": 706}, {"i": 707}, {"i": 708}, {"i": 709}, {"i": 710}, {"i": 711}, {"i": 712}], "expected_headings": [[1, "How to Use This Huge Guide"], [1, "Introduction"], [1, "Quick Start: Do This First"], [2, "Do You Think in Words?"], [1, "What I Mean by Hypnosis"], [1, "Protection From Hypnotists"], [1, "The Most Extreme Example"], [2, "Keep Your Adult in Charge"], [1, "Affirmations Done Right"], [1, "Undo Accidental Affirmations"], [1, "Hypnosis Evidence"], [1, "What It's For, and Not For"], [1, "Forget Left Brain/Right Brain"], [1, "You're Better Than the Pros"], [1, "A Useful Map of the Mind"], [2, "Start From the Whole"], [1, "Become a Trustworthy Adult"], [2, "The Nurturer"], [2, "The Protector"], [2, "When to Stop Scanning"], [2, "The Guide"], [2, "No Adult Yet? Borrow One"], [2, "Child Speaks, You Steer"], [2, "Love First, Trust Later"], [2, "Instead of Bla